# SPA fallback. The router is hand-rolled over the History API, so /play,
# /results, /archive, /about and /game/:id are not real files. Without this a
# static host 404s on a direct load, a refresh mid-game, or any shared link —
# which is every link the share card produces.
# 200 (not 301) so the URL stays intact for the router to read.
# Asset folders must 404 properly. The catch-all below was returning the 25KB
# HTML shell for a missing icon or font, which an <img> then fails to decode —
# wasteful, and it hides a genuinely missing file behind a confusing symptom.
/emoji/*   /emoji/:splat   404
/fonts/*   /fonts/:splat   404
/assets/*  /assets/:splat  404

/*    /index.html   200
